      "writtenOn": "2026-09-11T17:16:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for all that!\n\nWhile the `changes` cache should be disabled, the `changes_by_project` cache was designed to be a multi-primary safe replacement for `changes` and should offer some good perf improvement. It does have a warning in the release notes about [issue 380898784](https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/380898784), which could be applicable to your env (but I\u0027m also not clear on the failure case reported there).\n\nDo you have `core.usePerRequestRefCache\u003dtrue`?",
      "parentUuid": "226fe7e4_4dccbf2b",
      "revId": "fdd62f4067e23bcd3c643df1d65aa577f3504ba4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
